  "review": {
    "en": "An old man reads too many romances and rides out to be a knight, with a practical farmer at his side. What begins as parody turns into a long conversation between two people who change each other, and in the second part the characters know they are in a book. Much of what novels have done since is already here, done with warmth.",
    "zh": "一位老人读骑士小说读得太多，便骑马出门做骑士，身边跟着一个讲求实际的农夫。起初是戏仿，后来变成两个人长长的对话，彼此改变；到了第二部，人物甚至知道自己身在书中。此后小说做过的许多事，这里已经做过，而且做得很温暖。"
